
# skill

## behavior
- label: grill-with-facts turns plan-grilling conversations into durable .facts entries instead of chat-only notes
  command: grep -q 'durable outcomes' SKILL.md && grep -q 'facts add' SKILL.md
  tags: [implemented]

## companion-skills
- label: grill-with-facts explains when to use facts-refine, facts-implement, and facts-discover without replacing those lifecycle skills
  command: grep -q 'facts-refine' SKILL.md && grep -q 'facts-implement' SKILL.md && grep -q 'facts-discover' SKILL.md
  tags: [implemented]

# repository

## docs
- label: the repository README tells users what the skill does, when to use it, and how it relates to the facts lifecycle
  command: grep -q 'grill-with-facts' README.md && grep -q 'facts lifecycle' README.md && grep -q 'when to use it' README.md
  tags: [implemented]
- label: README section headings use lowercase style
  command: ! grep -qE '^## [A-Z]' README.md
  tags: [implemented]

## examples
- label: the repository includes a compact example showing a user answer becoming spec-tagged and draft-tagged facts
  command: grep -q '@spec' examples/grilling-session.md && grep -q '@draft' examples/grilling-session.md
  tags: [implemented]

## scope
- label: the skill repo has no package-manager dependency or generated build step
  command: test ! -f package.json && test ! -f bun.lock && test ! -f pnpm-lock.yaml && test ! -f package-lock.json
  tags: [implemented]
